# Per-service Redis ACL (ADR-0004 §8). DEV ONLY passwords; rendered by render-acl.sh at container start.
# One user per service: its own key prefixes (values, generation counters, single-flight locks), its own
# invalidation channel plus its own `<svc>:*` channel namespace (P15: reco fans SSE pushes out over
# reco:acct:<id>, A-87), and only the commands dexter-cache and that fan-out need. psubscribe is there because
# Spring's RedisMessageListenerContainer takes a PATTERN subscription (reco:acct:*) rather than one per account -
# `subscribe` alone is not enough for it, which reco's own StreamIT proves by failing to start without it. Reads/writes/locks/bumps are Lua scripts,
# so the commands they call (get set incr pexpire pttl unlink) must be listed too. No KEYS, FLUSH*, CONFIG, DEL.
# ping/info: Boot's Redis health indicator; client|setinfo/setname: Lettuce's connection handshake.
# dexter-test (RedisAclIT, DemoApp) applies this exact line with ACL SETUSER, so tests prove it is sufficient.
user {{svc}} on >{{pw}} resetkeys ~{{svc}}:* ~gen:{{svc}}:* ~lock:{{svc}}:* resetchannels &cache:inv:{{svc}} &{{svc}}:* -@all +get +set +incr +pexpire +pttl +unlink +scan +eval +evalsha +publish +subscribe +psubscribe +unsubscribe +punsubscribe +ping +info +client|setinfo +client|setname
